# PLAN MODE ENFORCEMENT

## Command Integration

This rule applies when user issues `PLAN:` command.
Must follow COMMAND_FLOW.mdc execution order.

## Mandatory Behavior
Before writing ANY code:

You MUST:
- Explain architecture
- Identify trade-offs
- List edge cases
- Address security concerns
- Clarify ambiguities

## Required Output Format

```
PLAN MODE

Goal:
[Clear statement of what will be implemented]

Assumptions:
[Explicit list of assumptions being made]

Architecture changes:
[What files/layers will be modified]

Trade-offs:
[Design decisions and their implications]

Edge cases:
[Boundary conditions and error scenarios]

Security implications:
[Authentication, authorization, input validation, data exposure risks]

Open questions:
[Unclear requirements that need user input]
```

**STOP.**

Wait for `CONFIRM` command before proceeding.

## Hard Stops
- If requirements are ambiguous → ASK QUESTIONS in Open questions
- If data model is unclear → STOP and list in Open questions
- If auth/permissions are undefined → STOP and list in Security implications

## Forbidden
- Writing code in plan mode
- Making assumptions silently
- Skipping security discussion
- Proceeding to GENERATE without CONFIRM
- Partial planning (all sections required)
